# Phase discipline

Read [docs/master-spec.md](docs/master-spec.md) and the current phase doc before changing code.

Work only on the current phase. Phase 1 through Phase 11 are complete. See [docs/phase-11.md](docs/phase-11.md). Locked sequence: [docs/roadmap.md](docs/roadmap.md). Fly.io is accepted and parked ([docs/phase-fly.md](docs/phase-fly.md)). Do not start Hyperliquid until Click asks.

Feature work happens on `develop`. Merge to `main` only when the user is ready for production.

Phase 11 is the first managing playbook. Type `dca` on the desk. Same `futures_*` ledger and `runFuturesCommand`. The app owns orders and exits. Signals only arm. Stacked playbooks, one per contract and side. The engine worker claims **one desk at a time** (Postgres leases). Do not call private exchange APIs from the browser. Paper accounts still use the in-app ledger.

Do not create later-phase tables or speculative architecture. Do not start Hyperliquid, copy trading, scale-in, MEXC, or onboarding wizard refine until Click starts that roadmap item. Standing unordered notes: [docs/click-list.md](docs/click-list.md). Hyperliquid is roadmap 2 ([docs/phase-hyperliquid.md](docs/phase-hyperliquid.md)). Scale-in / position builder is roadmap 6. See [docs/phase-onboarding.md](docs/phase-onboarding.md) (roadmap 9).

Keep dependencies minimal. Prefer the simplest solution that satisfies the current phase.

Stop at the end of the phase. After acceptance criteria pass, report results and wait for instruction.
